<title>UK: FORECAST - Reuters EMU survey - Criteria forecasts.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Reuters EMU survey - Criteria forecasts.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Five of the six countries expected to form the launch pad for a single currency are well on their way to meeting the required criteria, but Germany may lag behind, a Reuters survey showed on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Italy is on course to fulfil as many of the economic yardsticks for European economic and monetary union (EMU) as Germany, but analysts predicted Italy's entry may be delayed because of the weight of German public opinion against a euro that includes the lira from the start.</p>
<p>Reuters surveyed 32 economists across Europe between February 5 and 10 to predict each country's perfomance on the Maastricht criteria for 1997. A summary of the results follows.</p>
